# Style Rules

## Formatting
- 4-space indent, no tabs.
- Imports: `java.*`, then `javax.*`/`jakarta.*`, then third-party, then `com.example.*`. No wildcards except for static imports of test matchers.
- Trailing newline at EOF.
- Spotless + Google Java Format enforced by `mvn verify`.

## Naming
- Classes: `PascalCase`. Methods/fields: `camelCase`. Constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`.
- Tests: `methodName_whenCondition_thenOutcome`.
- Packages: lower-case, singular feature name (`posts`, `comments`, not `post`, `Posts`).

## Records vs Classes
- DTOs → **records** with validation annotations on components:
  ```java
  public record PostDto(
      UUID id,
      @NotBlank @Size(max = 200) String title,
      @NotBlank String body,
      @NotBlank String author,
      Instant createdAt
  ) {}
  ```
- Entities → **mutable classes** (JPA limitation). Use Lombok `@Getter`, `@Setter`, `@NoArgsConstructor(access = PROTECTED)`, `@AllArgsConstructor`.

## Lombok Usage
- Allowed: `@RequiredArgsConstructor`, `@Getter`, `@Setter`, `@NoArgsConstructor`, `@AllArgsConstructor`, `@Builder` (sparingly).
- Forbidden: `@Data` on entities (generates `equals`/`hashCode` from all fields → breaks JPA), `@Slf4j` cargo-culted everywhere (only where you actually log).

## Imports & Visibility
- Default to **package-private**. Public is opt-in: controllers, DTOs, the `BlogApplication` class, `shared/` types. Everything else stays package-private until something outside the package needs it.
- Repository interfaces and JPA impls are package-private.

## Null Discipline
- Optional<T> for "may be absent" return types from repositories.
- Service throws `NotFoundException` rather than returning `null` or empty `Optional` to controllers.
- Never return `null` from a controller method. Use `ResponseEntity.noContent()` for 204.

## Comments
- Default: no comments. Names carry the meaning.
- Exception: a single short line when the *why* is non-obvious (a JPA quirk, a workaround).
